---
import ServiceGuide from '../components/ServiceGuide.astro';
const URL_ = 'https://liverpoolemergencyplumber.co.uk/toilet-repair-liverpool';
const TEL = 'tel:01515580334';
const PHONE = '0151 558 0334';

const packages = [
  { id: 'weekday', tier: 'Weekday repair', popular: true, name: 'Toilet repair, first hour', price: '£120', unit: 'weekdays 9am–4pm, inc VAT',
    points: ['No call-out fee', 'Most flush and fill valve faults fixed in the first hour', 'Parts priced before we fit them', '12-month guarantee on our work'] },
  { id: 'out-of-hours', tier: 'Evenings, nights, weekends', name: 'Out-of-hours toilet repair', price: '£150', unit: 'first hour, inc VAT',
    points: ['Toilet overflowing or leaking now', 'Typically with you within 30 minutes', 'No call-out fee', 'Extra time priced before we carry on'] },
  { id: 'new-toilet', tier: 'Supply and fit', name: 'New toilet supplied and fitted', price: '£250', from: true, unit: 'inc VAT',
    points: ['Standard close-coupled toilet and seat', 'New pan connector and seals', 'Old toilet taken away', 'Fixed written price before we start'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does a toilet repair cost in Liverpool?', a: 'Our first hour is £120 including VAT on weekdays, 9am to 4pm. Evenings, nights and weekends are £150, and bank holidays are £180. There is no call-out fee. Most flush and fill valve faults are fixed in that first hour. Parts are priced before we fit them.' },
  { q: 'Do you unblock toilets?', a: 'No. We do not offer blocked toilet or drain clearing. If the water rises in the bowl and drains away slowly, that is a blockage, so you need a drainage company. If the toilet will not flush because the handle, button or valve is broken, that is a repair, and we can fix it.' },
  { q: 'Why does my toilet keep running?', a: 'Usually the flush valve seal is worn, so water leaks into the pan all the time. Or the fill valve does not shut off, so the cistern overfills into the overflow. Both are common, quick fixes.' },
  { q: 'Why is my toilet not flushing?', a: 'Most often the handle linkage, the button cable or the chain has snapped or slipped off. It can also be a broken flush valve, or no water coming into the cistern. Do the simple checks on this page first. If it is still not flushing, call us.' },
  { q: 'Why does my toilet have a weak flush?', a: 'The cistern may not fill high enough, or the flush valve may not lift fully. A worn siphon in an older lever toilet is another cause. We set the water level and repair or replace the part.' },
  { q: 'Why is water on the floor around my toilet?', a: 'The usual causes are the pan connector at the back, the seal between the cistern and the pan, or the pipe feeding the cistern. Condensation can look like a leak too. We find the source before we fix anything.' },
  { q: 'Is a running toilet an emergency?', a: 'Not usually, unless it is overflowing onto the floor. But it wastes water and can push up a metered water bill. Turn off the isolation valve if you can, and book a weekday visit at £120.' },
  { q: 'Can you fix a concealed cistern?', a: 'Often, yes. Most back-to-wall and wall-hung toilets have an access panel or a removable flush plate. If there is no way in, we tell you before we cut or remove anything.' },
  { q: 'Do you repair old high-level chain toilets?', a: 'Yes. Many older Liverpool terraces still have them. The chain, the lever and the valve inside can usually be repaired or replaced.' },
  { q: 'Should I repair or replace my toilet?', a: 'Repair it if the pan and cistern are sound. Replace it if the pan or cistern is cracked, parts are no longer made, or you want a more modern, water-saving toilet. A new toilet supplied and fitted is from £250.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take to fit a new toilet?', a: 'A like-for-like swap usually takes 2 to 3 hours. Moving the toilet, or a back-to-wall or wall-hung toilet, takes longer. We give you a fixed written price first.' },
  { q: 'Can you fit a toilet I have bought?', a: 'Yes. Tell us the make and model when you call, and we will give you the price before we start.' },
  { q: 'Do I pay extra for parts?', a: 'Yes, parts are on top of the labour. We always tell you the part price before we fit it, so there are no surprises.' },
  { q: 'Can you do other small jobs on the same visit?', a: 'Yes. Many small jobs fit in our first hour. Make a list, such as a dripping tap and a running toilet, and we will tell you the price before we start.' },
];
---

